-- title:
--   Ogg's unit and the components of the fibre at p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a positive integer with $p \mid M$ but $p^{2} \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ be a subgroup containing every unit that becomes $1$ under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$. Assume $j$-expansion condition `hj`, that `jqModC ℚ` (the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the integral $j$-numerator) lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the relevant ratios of integral forms, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport datum of type `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for the two-chart integral model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over `R p`. Then there is an element $v$ of the finite-chart coordinate algebra `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj` $\subseteq$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` whose Laurent expansion is either `modularUnitSeries p` $= \Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{p})$ or $p^{12}\,(\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{p}))^{-1}$, with the following property: for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed, every ring homomorphism $\rho :$ `R p` $\to A$ whose composition with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map, every point $y$ of the fibre of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` over $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the residue map `(IsLocalRing.residue ↥A).comp ρ`, and every prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj`: if the first projection of the fibre sends $y$ to the image of $\mathfrak{q}$ under the finite-chart immersion `ιFin p (ΓM M H) hj`, and $v \notin \mathfrak{q}$, then $y$ lies in the image of the component morphism $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,\rho\,0$ and not in the image of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,\rho\,1$.
--
--   This is the dictionary relating Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{p})$ to the two components of the fibre at $p$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ when $p$ exactly divides $M$: non-vanishing of the unit at a point of the finite chart pins the point to the component indexed $0$ and off the component indexed $1$. It is used in the analysis of crossing points and of the smooth locus of the special fibre, for instance by the results producing two-sided pools of closed primes in the smooth locus.
